L0245: Public Rust surface could forge an invariant

A public field or construction path would let safe Rust create data with erased evidence or mutate invariant-dependent fields without rechecking them. Hide the fields behind checked constructors and methods. Erasure must not grant the Rust caller a way to manufacture a proven invariant.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/pub_evidence_field.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```locus
// The export boundary, for a struct: a `pub` struct that carries evidence
// has every field private. A `pub` evidence field could be written with a
// marker, and a `pub` data field could be changed under the evidence that
// speaks of it; either way the value no longer means what its type says.
#[terminates] #[no_panic] #[no_io]
logic fn within_limit(failures: Int) -> Prop {
    prop!(failures <= 3)
}

pub struct Lock {
    failures: u8,
    pub bounded: @within_limit(failures),
}

pub struct Percent {
    pub value: u8,
    in_range: @(value <= 100),
}

// Evidence at depth: `Inner` is validated, so `Outer` may hold one in a
// `pub` field; `Open` is not, so `Holder` may not.
pub struct Inner {
    value: u8,
    in_range: @(value <= 100),
}

pub struct Outer {
    pub inner: Inner,
}

struct Open {
    value: u8,
    pub in_range: @(value <= 100),
}

pub struct Holder {
    pub open: Open,
}

// Not exported: a `pub(crate)` struct may carry evidence in a `pub` field,
// since only the generated crate sees it.
pub(crate) struct Carried {
    pub failures: u8,
    pub bounded: @within_limit(failures),
}
```

Language, as built: [1.23:1](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.23:1).
